From af656fbe6f43f84e4bccf26596c774c57b92064a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:43:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Noah-MP: take the latent heats from the host

Noah-MP charges the land its own latent heats for the water it evaporates
or sublimates (hvap = 2.5104e6, hsub = 2.844e6 J/kg), but the vapour enters
the atmosphere carrying the host's (con_hvap = 2.5e6; con_hvap + con_hfus
= 2.83358e6 from ice). The land therefore pays 0.4 % more latent energy
than its water carries into the atmosphere. This is the energy side of the
water-flux fix in noahmpdrv (cf. NCAR/ccpp-physics#582).

hvap, hsub and hfus become module variables (soil and glacier modules),
set at the start of noahmpdrv_run from its con_hvap and con_hfus arguments
(hsub = con_hvap + con_hfus), with the old values as defaults. The run
phase already receives both, from CCPP and from NOAA-EMC/noahmp's land
component alike, so no interface changes.

Measured with in-model meters (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, 24 h, 1.77M soil
column-steps): the land paid +0.131 W/m2 per land column more than its
vapour carries (0.41 % of the 31.8 W/m2 land latent heat flux, one-signed);
with the fix exactly 0. Water is unchanged.
